# func/date/dt_coer (id 358): text-to-date coercion of the date function arguments, between dt_abi's dispatch
# and the core. Entered at PC 0 from dt_abi with A B C = arguments, T0 / N1 = core selector, T9 = core id,
# T10 = core PC, T2 = 64 + fid, N0 = n. Finds the first text argument (A unless DATEVALUE or TIMEVALUE,
# B if n >= 1, C unless DATEDIF) and calls the parser in coercion mode (dv_ent 354, T0 = 2) with LR 358,
# LP = slot; the parser chain keeps every word but A and STATUS, so A's old value and the core T0 are parked
# in AS AR1 AC1. PC 1..3 (return): the result goes to slot LP, A and T0 come back from AS AR1 AC1, then the
# same search runs again. No text left: next = T9, PC = T10, LR 257, LP 0 (as dt_abi set them).
# Note: weights/func/date/dt_coer.md.
